From: RoboParty <2321901849@qq.com>
Date: Tue, 03 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: arm64: dts: rk3588-orangepi-5-plus: prefer sink for USB-C

On an independently powered board the default "source" preference makes
the Type-C port try to source 5V into a host PC, which can trip the host
port protection and prevent the port from ever enumerating as a device.
Prefer "sink" so the port behaves as a USB device.

---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-orangepi-5-plus.dts | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-orangepi-5-plus.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-orangepi-5-plus.dts
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-orangepi-5-plus.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-orangepi-5-plus.dts
@@ -205,7 +205,7 @@
 			op-sink-microwatt = <10>;
 			source-pdos = <PDO_FIXED(5000, 1400, PDO_FIXED_USB_COMM)>;
 			sink-pdos = <PDO_FIXED(5000, 10, PDO_FIXED_USB_COMM)>;
-			try-power-role = "source";
+			try-power-role = "sink";
 
 			ports {
 				#address-cells = <1>;
-- 
Armbian
